---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const page = {
  title: "Write XZ, gzip, Zstandard, and bzip2 disk images — Bootable",
  description: "Write XZ, gzip, Zstandard, and bzip2 disk images without manually extracting them, with expanded-size preflight and read-back verification.",
  ogTitle: "Write compressed disk images directly",
  ogDescription: "Expanded-size preflight, streaming decompression, cancellation, and read-back verification.",
  ogType: "article",
  current: "guide",
  doc: { label: "Safety", href: "https://github.com/debpalash/bootable/blob/main/docs/safety.md" },
  crumbs: [{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Guides", href: "/guides.html" }, { label: "Compressed images" }],
};
---
<Layout {...page}>
<main class="guide-main">
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={page.crumbs} />
      <article>
        <header class="guide-hero"><p class="eyebrow">XZ · gzip · Zstandard · bzip2</p><h1>Write compressed disk images directly.</h1><p class="lede">Bootable measures the expanded image, streams it to removable media, and verifies the expanded target bytes.</p></header>
        <div class="guide-body">
          <div class="guide-content">
            <h2 id="formats">Supported formats</h2>
            <p>Bootable recognizes XZ, gzip, Zstandard, and bzip2 around raw disk images and hybrid ISOs. You can open a local file or use a catalog download. Manual extraction is not required.</p>

            <h2 id="preflight">Expanded-size preflight</h2>
            <p>The compressed file size is not used for drive capacity checks. Bootable fully measures the decompressed stream during inspection, then builds the write plan with the expanded byte count.</p>
            <p>This extra inspection pass catches truncated or invalid compressed sources before the target is erased and prevents a small archive from being planned against a card that cannot hold its contents.</p>

            <h2 id="write">Streaming write</h2>
            <ol>
              <li>Open the compressed image and wait for inspection.</li>
              <li>Select a removable drive larger than the measured expanded size.</li>
              <li>Review both the source file and expanded byte count.</li>
              <li>Confirm erasure and start the write.</li>
              <li>Leave the media connected through read-back verification.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>Decompression feeds the writer directly. Bootable does not need to keep a second, fully extracted image beside the archive.</p>

            <h2 id="integrity">Two different integrity checks</h2>
            <p>A publisher checksum, when available, validates the compressed file you downloaded. Post-write verification validates the expanded byte stream written to the target. These checks cover different stages and are reported separately.</p>

            <h2 id="failure">Cancellation and failure</h2>
            <p>A decompression error stops the operation. Cancellation is checked during inspection and writing. Any interrupted target is marked incomplete and needs a full rewrite.</p>
            <div class="guide-callout"><p><strong>Keep enough local free space for the download.</strong> Manual extraction is unnecessary, but the compressed source still needs a complete local file.</p></div>

            <section class="related-guides"><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href="/raspberry-pi-image-writer">Write a Raspberry Pi image</a></li><li><a href="/write-iso-to-usb">Write a local ISO to USB</a></li><li><a href="/verify-bootable-usb">Compare checksum and read-back results</a></li></ul></section>
            <div class="guide-cta"><h2>Write compressed media</h2><p>Supported in both the desktop app and terminal interface.</p><a class="button primary" href="/download">Download Bootable</a></div>
          </div>
          <aside class="guide-aside"><strong>On this page</strong><ul><li><a href="#formats">Formats</a></li><li><a href="#preflight">Expanded-size check</a></li><li><a href="#write">Streaming write</a></li><li><a href="#integrity">Integrity checks</a></li><li><a href="#failure">Failure handling</a></li></ul></aside>
        </div>
      </article>
</main>
</Layout>
